

# 📄 TRD: AI Job Application Autofill + Smart CV Personalization Platform

---

## 1. Overview

**Product Name:** AutoApply AI
**Goal:**
Automate job applications from links, dynamically tailor resumes (CVs) per Job Description (JD), and generate ATS-friendly, well-designed PDFs.

---

## 2. Core Problem

Users currently:

* Manually fill repetitive job forms
* Manually tweak resumes per JD
* Struggle with ATS optimization
* Maintain multiple resume versions

---

## 3. Solution Summary

A system that:

1. Takes job links (LinkedIn, Greenhouse, Lever, etc.)
2. Extracts JD
3. Modifies base resume intelligently (without losing identity)
4. Generates ATS + themed CVs
5. Autofills applications via browser automation
6. Supports multiple LLMs + API keys (BYOK)

---

## 4. Key Technologies

### 4.1 Browser Automation

* Use: browser-use
* Purpose:

  * Navigate job links
  * Extract JD
  * Fill forms
  * Upload CV
* Why:

  * Agentic browser control
  * Works with LLM loops

---

### 4.2 Design + CV Engine

* Use: open-design
* Capabilities:

  * 19 composable design skills + 71 design systems ([GitHub][1])
  * Export to PDF/HTML/PPTX ([Trendshift][2])
* Purpose:

  * Generate ATS-friendly CVs
  * Themed CVs (modern, minimal, corporate)
  * Portfolio-style resumes

---

### 4.3 LLM Layer (BYOK)

* Supported:

  * OpenAI
  * Anthropic
  * Gemini
  * Local (Ollama)
* Reason:

  * open-design is model-agnostic (BYOK) ([GitHub][1])

---

## 5. System Architecture

```
Frontend (Next.js)
    ↓
Backend API (Node.js / FastAPI)
    ↓
-------------------------------
|   AI Orchestrator Layer     |
|-----------------------------|
| - JD Extractor             |
| - Resume Personalizer      |
| - ATS Optimizer            |
| - Cover Letter Generator   |
-------------------------------
    ↓
-------------------------------
| Browser Agent Layer        |
| (browser-use)             |
| - Navigate job links       |
| - Autofill forms           |
| - Upload CV                |
-------------------------------
    ↓
-------------------------------
| Design Engine              |
| (open-design)             |
| - CV templating            |
| - PDF export               |
-------------------------------
```

---

## 6. Features

---

### 6.1 Job Link Processing

**Input:**

* Job URL

**Flow:**

1. Open link via browser-use
2. Extract:

   * Title
   * Company
   * Skills
   * Experience
3. Normalize JD

---

### 6.2 Resume Personalization Engine

**Input:**

* Base Resume (JSON structured)
* JD

**Output:**

* Tailored Resume

**Rules:**

* Do NOT fabricate experience
* Rephrase using JD keywords
* Highlight matching skills
* Adjust bullet points priority

---

### 6.3 ATS Optimization Engine

* Keyword density optimization
* Section standardization:

  * Experience
  * Skills
  * Projects
* Avoid:

  * Tables
  * Complex layouts

---

### 6.4 CV Design Engine

Using open-design:

**Modes:**

1. ATS Mode (simple, text-first)
2. Modern Mode
3. Creative Mode
4. Portfolio Mode

**Output:**

* PDF (primary)
* HTML (optional)

---

### 6.5 Autofill Engine

Using browser-use:

**Steps:**

1. Detect form fields
2. Map fields → resume data
3. Fill:

   * Name
   * Email
   * Experience
4. Upload generated CV
5. Submit application

---

### 6.6 Cover Letter Generator

* Uses JD + resume
* Optional toggle

---

### 6.7 Model & API Configuration

User UI:

* Select model:

  * GPT / Claude / Gemini / Local
* Enter API key
* Save securely (encrypted)

---

## 7. Data Model

---

### 7.1 Resume Schema

```json
{
  "name": "",
  "email": "",
  "skills": [],
  "experience": [
    {
      "company": "",
      "role": "",
      "bullets": []
    }
  ],
  "projects": []
}
```

---

### 7.2 Job Schema

```json
{
  "title": "",
  "company": "",
  "skills_required": [],
  "description": ""
}
```

---

## 8. Personalization Algorithm

---

### Step 1: JD Parsing

* Extract keywords
* Cluster skills

### Step 2: Resume Matching

* Score each bullet point vs JD

### Step 3: Rewrite

* Inject keywords
* Improve phrasing

### Step 4: Rank

* Reorder experience points

---

## 9. UX Flow

1. Upload base resume
2. Paste job links (bulk supported)
3. Select:

   * Model
   * CV theme
4. Click **Apply All**
5. System:

   * Generates CV
   * Applies automatically
6. Dashboard shows:

   * Status
   * Submitted / Failed

---

## 10. Non-Functional Requirements

* Scalability: async job queue
* Security:

  * Encrypt API keys
  * No resume data leaks
* Performance:

  * <10 sec CV generation
* Reliability:

  * Retry failed applications

---

## 11. Edge Cases

* CAPTCHA → fallback manual
* Unsupported job portals
* File upload failures
* Anti-bot detection

---

## 12. Future Enhancements

* Chrome extension
* Job recommendation engine
* Interview prep integration
* Analytics (success rate)

---

## 13. Risks

* Anti-bot detection (major)
* JD parsing inaccuracies
* Over-optimization hurting authenticity

---

## 14. MVP Scope

* Single job apply
* 1 CV theme
* 1 model (OpenAI)
* Basic autofill

---

## 15. Advanced Version (What makes this 🔥)

* Multi-model switching
* Multi-theme CV generation
* Agent-based auto apply loop
* Resume memory + learning system

---

## 16. Differentiators

* Combines:

  * Automation (browser-use)
  * Design (open-design)
  * Intelligence (LLMs)
* Local-first possibility (via open-design philosophy) ([GitHub][1])

---

## 17. Sample Flow (End-to-End)

```
User → Paste LinkedIn job URL
→ JD extracted
→ Resume optimized
→ CV generated (PDF)
→ Browser agent fills form
→ CV uploaded
→ Application submitted
```

